declared once, structured so that a pitch, a landing page and an editorial
standard can all derive from it — and so that `fid advise` can ask whether it is
falsifiable. Run `fid thesis` to see it and what is still unanswered about it.

This file is for what a structured claim cannot hold: the context, the history,
the constraints you are working under, the things you decided not to do. Write
as much or as little as you want. Nothing derives from this file, which is
exactly why the claim does not live in it.

